+  first face-to-face mate's fixture normal, + counter-clockwise looking
+  down it; else setup +Z), on wrapped lines above short row labels the
+  label column cannot truncate. A fixture pick while a part face is
+  wanted adds "hide the fixture (eye) to pick part faces hidden in it".
 - **MCP:** `locate_part` (mates by `list_features` ids, offset, turn,
   move), and `list_features` now lists a fixture's features too so its
   face ids can be named.

From 18802064ec64250012d064a4717eba2f431985e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:20:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(app): turning a part keeps a square stock square

A Model-page turn (plain MoveModel) now uses the #561 square-stock rule
the locate already used: a box or cylinder stock square to the setup
keeps its orientation and is re-fitted round the turned part with the
allowance it had on each side, quarter turns included. A move that does
not turn the part carries the stock rigidly exactly as before; copied or
already-turned stocks still follow rigidly. MoveModel::locating is now
the same move as MoveModel::new.

Fixes #571

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
